```yaml
spec:
  grid: 12-14 rows x 11-15 cols
  background: black (0)
  rectangles:
    count: 2-4 solid filled axis-aligned rectangles
    height: 3-7
    width: 3-8
    colors: each from {1, 2, 3} (not teal=8); 2-3 distinct colors total [observed]
    multiple_same_color: allowed (test has 2 rects sharing a color)
    separation: >=1 bg cell gap between any two bounding boxes
    border_touching: rects may touch grid edges
    no_teal_in_input: input contains no teal (8) pixels
  transform:
    for each rectangle, replace its strict 1-pixel-inset interior with teal (8)
    border ring (1px) retains original color; background unchanged
    every rect is >=3x3 so interior is always non-empty

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct (constraints are simple enough for forward generation)
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size H in [12,14], W in [11,15]
    2. Fill grid with black (0)
    3. Pick N in [2,4] rectangles
    4. For each rect, pick height in [3,7], width in [3,8], color from {1,2,3}
    5. Place rects on grid with >=1 cell gap between all pairs and within bounds; retry placement if overlap
    6. Fill each rect's bbox solidly with its color
    7. Build output by copying input, then for each rect set interior (r0+1..r1-1, c0+1..c1-1) to teal (8)
```
</generation_spec>
